WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.945
CompTIA Network Plus, domain 2, Network implementation, which is 20 percent of the exam.

00:00:07.945 --> 00:00:10.580
This lesson covers objective 2 point 1.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:13.823
Explain characteristics of routing technologies.

00:00:13.823 --> 00:00:16.661
Inside it, first hop redundancy protocols.

00:00:16.661 --> 00:00:18.620
Which one can share the load?

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:24.150
Three clients share two gateways for redundancy.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:30.318
With H S R P or V R R P, one router is active, or master, and carries all the traffic.

00:00:30.318 --> 00:00:32.280
The other waits as a standby.

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:35.617
G L B P, which is Cisco proprietary, changes that.

00:00:35.617 --> 00:00:41.770
It hands out different gateways to different clients, so both routers forward traffic at the same time.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:48.627
HSRP and VRRP normally send everything through one active router.

00:00:48.627 --> 00:00:51.971
G L B P adds load balancing across the gateways.

00:00:51.971 --> 00:00:54.130
That's objective two point one.
